12
01:17:41,052 --> 01:17:47,052
Hotel Mumbai is a 2018 independent action thriller film directed by
Anthony Maras and co-written by Maras and John Collee.

13
01:24:09,473 --> 01:24:15,473
An Indian-Australian-American co-production, it is inspired by the 2009 documentary Surviving
Mumbai about the 2008 Mumbai attacks at the Taj Mahal Palace Hotel in India.

14
01:30:37,894 --> 01:30:43,894
The film stars Dev Patel, Armie Hammer, Nazanin Boniadi, Anupam Kher, Tilda
Cobham-Hervey, Jason Isaacs, Suhail Nayyar, Nagesh Bhosle, and Natasha Liu Bordizzo.

15
01:37:06,315 --> 01:37:12,315
The film premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on 7 September 2018, and had
its Australian premiere at the Adelaide Film Festival on 10 October 2018.

16
01:43:34,736 --> 01:43:40,736
The film was released in Australia and the United States on 14 and 22
March 2019, respectively, and in India on 29 November 2019.

17
01:50:03,157 --> 01:50:09,157
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship, mumbai (bombay),
india, based on true story, india, struggle for survival.

18
01:56:31,578 --> 01:56:37,578
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and intense.
